/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (FIRST \(For the Inspiration and Recognition of Science and Technology\) is an organization that runs robotics competitions for students ages five to eighteen. FIRST prepares them for the future through Science Technology Engineering and Mathematics \(STEM\). The FIRST robotics competition covers a league of high school students in which "Under strict rules, limited resources, and the guidance of volunteer mentors, including engineers, teachers, business professionals, parents, alumni and more, teams of students build and program robots to perform challenging tasks against a field of competitors. They must also raise funds, design a team "brand," hone teamwork skills, and perform community outreach." \(firstinspires.org\). The FIRST robotics competition season consists of a six-week build phase to accomplish conceptualization, design, fabrication, and testing of a robot that accomplishes a series of competitive sport-like tasks for points. The robot is operated autonomously through its internal programming and through radio control. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2 314 0 R 4]
>>
endobj
