/E (Our mission is to provide high school students, regardless of their prior experience, with the opportunity to delve into the world of robotics. As they progress through our program, they will develop the skills and mindset necessary to confidently address complex technical challenges and craft innovative solutions in diverse, fast-paced environments, ultimately contributing to the advancement of technology and shaping a brighter future. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E ( Team expenditures are an important part of managing a high school FIRST Robotics Competition \(FRC\) team, as they ensure that the team has the resources necessary to design, build, and compete with a successful robot. Major expenses include robot materials and components, such as motors, electronics, raw materials, tools, and mechanical parts, as well as registration fees for the year and competitions. Additional costs may include team apparel, safety equipment, software, and outreach activities within the community. Since FRC is an expensive program we rely on sponsorships, grants, and donations to cover these expenses. Careful budgeting and responsible spending help ensure that funds are used effectively, allowing all team members to participate and giving the team the best possible opportunity to succeed. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
